   "**NATO membership offered as compensation for land inverts the logic of deterrence** — a guarantee is worth most where the territory is most exposed, and this trade gives up the exposed part and guarantees the rest; the direct effect is a shorter, more defensible line, which is militarily coherent; the compound consequence is that the principle \"no gains from aggression\" is replaced by \"gains priced in alliance membership\" — a precedent every other revisionist border in the world can now cite, and one that Russia will argue was its own victory whatever the treaty says",
