  "hinge": "§8:42 does not forbid the negotiation — it commands that war be avoided *with all good and fair means*, and it identifies the test: whether the mean produces peace, freedom and harmony, or merely a pause in the destruction. A land-for-membership trade can pass that test, but only if it is written before it is announced. So write it: publish the draft's **security-guarantee annex** — what each of the thirty-two parliaments would be asked to ratify, with what obligation, triggered by what — and publish it **before** Shenzhen, because a guarantee drafted after a leaders' photograph will be drafted to fit the photograph. Give Europe's six-member team a **written mandate** from the twenty-seven, so the seat is a European decision and not an American indulgence. Publish the **referendum question and the map** that goes with it, so the electorate knows precisely what it is being asked to accept. And put the nuclear file on the table with its annexes attached: data exchange, inspection rights, a verification body, a date — because that is the only item in this week's diplomacy where all three men in the room have something to gain and nothing to concede but transparency."
