  "cause": "**The fight at COP31 is not about what the science says. It is about what day it is published.** Delegates in **Antalya**, where the summit runs from **9 to 20 November** under **Türkiye** and **Australia**, have turned the publication timetable of the **Intergovernmental Panel on Climate Change** into one of the conference's burning issues. The IPCC's assessment reports appear every five to seven years; the next round would cover the physical changes to the earth and greenhouse gas emissions. The timing matters because **2028** is a **stocktake** year — the five-yearly moment when nations assess collective progress and are expected to raise their pledges, the mechanism the *New York Times* calls *\"the engine of the Paris Agreement.\"* **Saudi Arabia, India and Russia** are among those pushing to delay the reports so that **at least two of them are published after 2028**. All three are among the largest fossil fuel exporters or importers, which is why the accusation has been made in the open. *\"Saudi Arabia is trying to destroy the I.P.C.C. in order to prevent the next global stocktake from using the accurate scientific data on fossil fuels,\"* said **Al Gore**, who is in Antalya. **This is the cheapest veto in the building, and it requires nobody to say the science is wrong.** A party that disputes findings must argue with them in public, in front of its own scientists, and lose. A party that merely moves the calendar loses nothing and wins a full cycle: a report published after the stocktake cannot inform it, and the next opportunity to inform the process arrives in **2033**. Meanwhile **António Guterres**, in his final climate summit speech, told the room *\"you cannot build peace on a burning planet\"*, and a study reported by *The Guardian* counted **more than 100 companies and groups linked to fossil fuels** represented at the summit — in a hall where the cover decision is due by **20 November**, and where the independent **Climate Action Tracker** reported on Thursday that progress has **stalled for five years**, leaving the world headed for an irrecoverable overshoot of 1.5°C toward roughly **1.8°C**. The instrument being re-timed is the only one that tells the stocktake what it is measuring.",
  "bullets": [
   "**Delaying the assessment is a veto on the evidence that costs the vetoing party nothing to cast** — no finding is disputed, no scientist is contradicted, no vote is lost; the direct effect is that the 2028 stocktake proceeds on the previous generation of science; the compound consequence is that the mechanism designed to ratchet ambition becomes a mechanism for ratifying self-reported inventories — and once the calendar is treated as negotiable, every future calendar is too, which converts a scientific institution into a second negotiating table where the oil exporters already have a seat",
   "**A five-year slip is not a delay, it is a lost ratchet** — pledges are raised at stocktakes, stocktakes are informed by assessments, and assessments arrive every five to seven years; the direct effect is that the round of pledges due in 2030 is written without the physics of the 2020s; the compound consequence is that the overshoot the IPCC has already declared likely will be managed with instruments calibrated before the last five years of record heat, record ocean temperatures and record emissions — so adaptation spending, insurance pricing and loss-and-damage allocation all lag the hazard by a full cycle, and the lag is chosen by the parties who profit from it",
   "**The countries asking for delay are the countries whose development paths the reports describe** — India's coal build-out, Russia's export dependence, Saudi Arabia's oil revenues; the direct effect is that the reports would land in the middle of their own transition decisions; the compound consequence is that the delay request is rational for each and catastrophic in aggregate, which is the defining structure of the climate problem and the reason a unanimous scientific calendar cannot be governed by consensus — an institution whose output schedule requires the assent of the parties it assesses will always be scheduled by its weakest assessee",
   "**Fossil-fuel presence in the hall is not corruption, it is the ordinary physics of a consensus body** — more than 100 linked companies and groups, 190 delegations, a host whose president celebrated two new oil fields two days before telling the summit that costs keep growing; the direct effect is that the industry's preference enters the process as a national position; the compound consequence is that the conference's legitimacy erodes among the parties who cannot afford to be cynical — the island states, the delta states, the states negotiating with a currency the room no longer accepts — and their withdrawal from the process is the outcome that costs everyone the most",
   "**A cover decision that mentions science without dating it will be read as a decision about science** — the text closes on 20 November; a paragraph reaffirming the IPCC's importance while leaving its timetable to \"further consultations\" achieves the delay without recording who asked for it; the direct effect is that no party is accountable for the slip; the compound consequence is that the summit's own success metric — the existence of an agreed text — is satisfied by the paragraph that removes the evidence, so the mechanism of failure is also the mechanism of applause"
  ],
  "verse": "Truly, kindheartedness and beneficence towards people of your kind (fellow human beings) is a clear sign (evidence) of your dignity… therefore give at all time in full measure (ampleness/sufficiency) and full weight (extent) and do not reduce the belongings (possessions) of people of your kind… just as you shall not foment chaos on Earth or unpeace amongst people of your kind (human beings); keep your world in all things in regulation so that you do not destroy it and your space (dwelling space).",
  "verseSrc": "Chapter 7, Verse 86",
  "hinge": "§7:86 sets two obligations side by side — do not reduce what belongs to others, and keep the world *in regulation* so that it is not destroyed. Re-timing the assessment does the second while pretending it is not doing the first: it removes the measurement that keeps the system in regulation, and the people whose belongings are reduced are the ones who live at the elevation the report would have described. The hinge is a date in the cover decision. Write the IPCC timetable into the text as a **fixed obligation** — publication of the physical-science and emissions reports **before** the 2028 stocktake, with the acceptance plenary scheduled and funded — and require that any request to move it be **recorded by name in an annex**, because a delay that must be signed is a delay somebody has to own. Then tie the stocktake's terms of reference to the **best available science**, including chapters accepted but not yet published, so that a missed deadline cannot be used as an argument for ignorance. Two paragraphs, both cheap, both closable on 20 November. The alternative is a summit that agrees the target, praises the science, and moves the report to the year after the decision it was written to inform."
